{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"An individual term of a series is the difference between two successive partial sums.\n\nIn particular, $\\displaystyle{{a}_{n}}={{S}_{n}}-{{S}_{n-1}}\\,$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\\displaystyle{{S}_{n}}-{{S}_{n-1}}\u0026=\\dfrac{3n}{3n+1}-\\dfrac{3(n-1)}{3(n-1)+1}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\displaystyle ~=\\frac{3n}{3n+1}-\\frac{3n-3}{3n-2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\displaystyle ~=\\frac{3n(3n-2)-(3n-3)(3n+1)}{(3n+1)(3n-2)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026\\displaystyle ~=\\frac{3}{(3n+1)(3n-2)}\n\\end{align}$\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"The $n\\text{th}$ partial sum of the series $\\sum\\limits_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{{a}_{n}}}$ is given by\n\n$\\displaystyle{{S}_{n}}=\\frac{3n}{3n+1}$.\n\n**Write a rule for ${{a}_{n}}$.**\n\n[[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"3/((3n+1)(3n-2))"}],"buttonSets":["basic"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
